===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|her}}, {{m|enm|heer}}, {{m|enm|hær}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hǣr}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hār}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hērą|t=hair}}.

Cognate with {{cog|stq|Hier|t=hair}}, {{cog|fy|hier|t=hair}}, {{cog|nl|haar|t=hair}}, {{cog|nds-de|Haar|t=hair}}, {{cog|de|Haar|t=hair}}, {{cog|sv|-}}, {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|no|hår|t=hair}}, {{cog|is|hár|t=hair}}. Eclipsed non-native {{noncog|enm|cheveler}}, {{m|enm|chevelere|t=hair}}, borrowed from {{noncog|fro|chevelëure|t=hair, head-hair, coiffure, wig}}.

The modern spelling with ''ai'' is not a regular representation of the vowel developed from Middle English. Rather, it is from {{inh|en|enm|here}} (haircloth) influenced by {{noncog|fro|haire}}.

